# The log viewer is a local tool and is deliberately not deployed.
#
# The log lives in Neon, not on Vercel, so the same DATABASE_URL that production
# writes to is the one `.env.local` reads. Running the dev server on a laptop
# shows real student data with no public endpoint and no secret to manage. There
# is nothing the deployed copy would add except a way to get it wrong.
demos/ask/log.html
api/log.js
# /beta: every class as its teacher sees it, over the same local-only api/log.js.
demos/build/beta.html

# The question-bank editor is a local tool. It writes demos/questions.js through
# the dev server's /api/questions, an endpoint that lives in tools/dev-server.js
# and is deliberately not one of the Vercel functions in api/. Deployed, the page
# would be a read-only form with a Save that could never work, so it is not
# deployed at all — and the page checks its own hostname besides.
demos/questions-cms.html

# The map's editor, for the same reason and through the same kind of endpoint
# (/api/mapcontent, also only in tools/dev-server.js). lib/mapcontent.js itself
# IS deployed — door-map.html reads it — but nothing that writes it is.
demos/map-cms.html

# The access-code admin: reads and writes the live database through an
# endpoint that exists only in tools/dev-server.js, and only for loopback.
demos/tools/codes.html
demos/tools/codes-api.js
# The builder's prompts, read the same way.
demos/tools/prompts.html
demos/tools/prompts-api.js

# The clip shelf, same reason and the same kind of endpoint (/api/clips, also
# only in tools/dev-server.js). It reaches the network and shells out to ffmpeg,
# neither of which a Vercel function here does. What it WRITES is deployed:
# nodegraph/clips/*.mp4 and their posters are what a student sees, and
# nodegraph/clips.js is the registry the map reads.
demos/clip-shelf.html

# The image clipper is a Chrome extension, not a page, and it is loaded
# unpacked from this folder. Same endpoint story as the shelf (/api/images, only
# in tools/dev-server.js). What it WRITES is deployed: nodegraph/images/* are
# what a student sees, and nodegraph/images.js is the registry the map reads.
demos/tools/clipper/

# Test benches and generated-app evals: for us, on the dev server. admin.html
# links them, so /admin has dead links in production; that is expected.
# Benches a public page links are NOT here and must stay deployed: the library's
# component cards (water-test, salmon-test, animalcell-test and the rest, plus
# graph-shell-test, which graph-test links), every /proteins/<key> page, and the
# prototypes capillary/pbf-test.html and sickle/fibre-test.html.
demos/tests/
demos/ask/ask-test.html
demos/ask/chat-test.html
demos/build/edit-test.html
demos/build/outline-test.html
demos/capillary/nanopore-test.html
demos/chain/glucose-chains-test.html
demos/chair/chair-test.html
demos/coupling/coupling-test.html
demos/diffusion/diffusion-test.html
demos/dna/codon-test.html
demos/energy/energy-test.html
demos/hemoglobin/crowd-test.html
demos/hemoglobin/surface-test.html
demos/hemoglobin/tube-test.html
demos/hexokinase/closure-test.html
demos/kit/hbond-test.html
demos/kit/kit-test.html
demos/kit/proteinbox-skin-test.html
demos/kit/ribbon-test.html
demos/lobes/lobes-test.html
demos/massaction/massaction-test.html
demos/membrane/atp-handoff-test.html
demos/membrane/chemiosmosis-test.html
demos/membrane/membrane-pump-test.html
demos/membrane/parts-test.html
demos/membrane/pump-test.html
demos/molecule-builder/builder-test.html
demos/proteins/rb69/rb69-test.html
demos/reaction/reaction-test.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Git integration honours this file too (demos/ask/log.html 404s in
# production), so every entry above and below keeps a file off the site however
# it deploys. The entries below matter most for a CLI deploy (`vercel --prod`
# from a laptop), which uploads the WORKING TREE, gitignored files included.

# The key. Gitignored, and that is not the same as vercelignored.
.env.local
.env*.local

# Agent worktrees: ~100 MB of full repo checkouts, including their own copies
# of everything above.
.claude/

# Installed per build from package.json; uploading them is slower and can ship
# a tree that does not match the manifest.
node_modules/
demos/node_modules/

.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# The viewer-compare bench. A weekly-use style reference that shares nothing
# with the lessons - CDN libraries, structures fetched from RCSB - and is meant
# to be liftable into its own repo. Nothing about it belongs on a student's URL.
# vercel.json also redirects the route away, as a second guard.
viewer-compare/

# Deposited structures. These are BAKER INPUTS - the bakers under */tools/ read
# them and write the .bin/.json the pages actually fetch, so the deploy needs
# none of them. They stay in git precisely because they are not reproducible on
# demand: a PDB entry gets superseded, an AlphaFold URL moves, and a re-bake
# months later would silently use a different structure than the one the lesson
# was checked against. Git is the pin.
#
# Four bench pages DO fetch one at runtime - folding-lab.html and
# folding-lab-ribbon.html (1VII), kit/ribbon-test.html (villin),
# hemoglobin/hemoglobin-inhouse.html (2HHB). All four are prototypes or test
# benches, used on the dev server, and none is a featured lesson. They break on
# the deployed site and nowhere else. vercel.json redirects the extension away
# as a second guard, as for viewer-compare/.
*.pdb

# Superseded lessons, kept as worked examples. folding-lab.html and
# folding-lab-ribbon.html were the protein-structure lesson before
# hemoglobin-lab.html took all four levels onto one molecule; both are tagged
# `reference` on admin.html. They still load folding/, so they are kept rather
# than deleted, but a student following a link into one would be reading a
# lesson this repo no longer stands behind.
demos/attic/

# Candidate triage: a script that greps a deposition's records and a page that
# looks at one in 3Dmol, both used while deciding whether a structure is worth
# a bake. The page loads an outside viewer from a CDN, which is exactly what a
# lesson must not do — rendering-modules.md's rule is about what ships, and
# nothing here does. Neither is linked from a lesson.
demos/proteins/tools/triage.html
